id: skill-of-the-watcher
name: Skill of the Watcher
order: 2
category: mind
importance: primary
description: >
  You are a divine being meant to watch over the universe or rule over it. The patience to observe others leads to you gaining critical information.
text: >
  Skill of the Watcher (Mind): You are a divine being meant to watch over the universe or rule over it. The patience to observe others leads to you gaining critical information.
  (1)-[Passive]: You can sense God Ki.
  (2)-[Passive]: Your minimum Action Cost for Combat Recovery is 1 Action.
  (3)-[Triggered]: Increase your Combat Rolls and Soak Value by 1(T) for the duration of any of your Counter Maneuvers.
  (4)-[Triggered]: At the end of the Combat Round, regain 2(bT) Life and Ki Points for each Counter Action you possess.
  (5)-[Triggered, 1/Round]: If you deal Damage with an Attacking Maneuver made through the Exploit Maneuver, or do not receive Damage from an Attacking Maneuver that you used the Defend Maneuver in response to, you may use the Power Up Maneuver as an Out-of-Sequence Maneuver.
  (6)-[Triggered/Start of Combat Round]: You may spend 1 Action to gain 2 Counter Actions.

---

# (1) God Ki "cannot be sensed": a Concealment Clash from one who senses it is not won outright (chat.mjs).
# (2) Combat Recovery's 2~3 Actions become 1~3.
# (5) Offered on the attack's card, to take or leave, once a Combat Round (chat.mjs offerWatcherPowerUp).
[passive]
allow sense.godKi;
combat-recovery.actionCost.minimum = 1;
allow powerUp.afterExploitOrDefend;

# (3) Offered in a window as you use any Counter Maneuver - the Defend, Exploit and Intervene Maneuvers, a Counter Unique
# Ability - and ticked, held for its duration (chat.mjs answerCounter): every roll and Damage of that exchange, the
# Out-of-Sequence Basic Attack an Exploit or a Cross Counter hands you among them. Over once you answer another attack,
# use a Maneuver of your own in sequence, or the turn passes.
[triggered/counter-maneuver]
combatRolls += 1(T);
soakValue += 1(T);

# (4) Armed from the Traits tab: as each Combat Round ends, before the Counter Actions come back.
[triggered/end-of-round]
life.value += 2(bT) * actions.counterLeft;
ki.value += 2(bT) * actions.counterLeft;

# (6) From the Combat Round's own card, its Action paid as it is taken.
[triggered/start-of-round, costs 1 action]
actions.counterGained += 2;
